  "index": 17,
  "response": "\nThis is a classic puzzle! The answer is 0.\n\nHere's why:\n\nLet's assume you have n unmatched socks in the drawer. You want to find out how many you need to pull out to get a match.\n\nIf you pull out 1 sock, you now have n-1 unmatched socks left. If you don't get a match, you'll still have n-1 unmatched socks after pulling out the second sock. And if you don't get a match with the second sock either, you'll still have n-2 unmatched socks after pulling out the third sock, and so on.\n\nSince you'll always have at least 1 unmatched sock left after pulling out any number of socks, the answer is that you never need to pull out more than 0 socks to get a match. Therefore, the number of socks you need to pull out to get a match is 0.",
